BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Create Your Signature Drag Look with Kurt Cumstain &amp\; Support 
 Palestine!
DTSTART:20260718T093000
DTEND:20260718T093000
UID:dffb772c1bfb12ff5870638951222a22@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:From Development to Details: A workshop on creating and/or dev
 eloping a signature look for your drag persona from idea to execution -PWY
 C! Pay what you can at the door! $5 contribution is required to register t
 o hold your place. We will be raffling off a free month at Kula Yoga studi
 o for one of the lucky participants. From Development to Details: Creating
  Your Signature Drag Look with Kurt Cumstain Discover how to create—or r
 efine—a signature look that authentically represents your drag persona. 
 This interactive 2.5-hour workshop guides participants through the creativ
 e process\, from initial inspiration and aesthetic research to bringing a 
 fully realized character to life through makeup and styling. Duration: 2 h
 ours 30 minutes Workshop Breakdown Hour 1: Character Development &amp\; Ae
 sthetic Research Explore methods for researching visual references and dev
 eloping a cohesive drag aesthetic. Learn how to define your drag persona&#
 x27\;s identity\, story\, and signature style. Discover techniques for tra
 nslating inspiration into a unique and recognizable look. Hour 2: Live Mak
 eup Demonstration Watch a step-by-step demonstration of how research and c
 haracter development inform makeup choices. Learn practical techniques for
  creating a signature face that aligns with your drag persona. Gain insigh
 t into the decision-making process behind a polished\, cohesive drag look.
  Final 30 Minutes: Q&amp\;A and Group Discussion Ask questions about chara
 cter development\, makeup\, and personal style. Share ideas and receive fe
 edback in an open\, supportive discussion. Leave with practical tools and 
 inspiration to continue developing your signature drag aesthetic. ‍
LOCATION:Kula Yoga Studio\, 304 Brunswick Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/create-your-signature-drag-look-with-kurt-
 cumstain-support-palestine
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:T4Beach
DTSTART:20260718T110000
DTEND:20260718T110000
UID:f46bfb43f43ea47871dd35f259caaa1e@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:🚨🌈PRIDE MONTH ALERT!🌈🚨 The event we’ve all been 
 waiting for - T4BEACH\, Toronto’s first ALL Trans Beach Day! Calling all
  Transfemmes\, Transmascs &amp\; everyone in between + beyond for a gorgeo
 us day in nature\, surrounded by community. Allies welcome! 🏳️‍⚧
 ️ When: July 18th 11AM - Sunset / July 19th Rain Date Where: Hanlan’s 
 Point Clothing Optional Beach We have generously been given 150 free ferry
  tickets by the @waterfrontbia to give out to the first batch of folks who
  show up! First come\, first serve. We’ll have team members waiting by t
 he side of the ferry ticket booths\, handing them out starting 10:30AM - 1
 2:30PM or until all tickets have been claimed. These tickets are reserved 
 for members of the Trans community only. We’ll be going all day until su
 nset so be sure to stay aware of ferry &amp\; water taxi departure times. 
 Last ferry from Hanlan’s Point leaves at 11:00PM. You can find ferry sch
 edules on the city of Toronto website. A reminder that Hanlan’s Point Be
 ach is both a public &amp\; clothing optional space. You will be in the pr
 esence of N*dists/Naturists of all walks of life &amp\; we ask that you be
  respectful of that. As this is a public beach\, we cannot be in control o
 f who enters the space so please be aware of your surroundings &amp\; stic
 k with your friends. We’ll be posting more info &amp\; details as time g
 oes on so make sure you follow our instagram page to stay up to date! ‍ 
 ‍
LOCATION:Hanlan&#x27\;s Point Beach\, Toronto Islands
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/t4beach
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Latine Book Club
DTSTART:20260718T110000
DTEND:20260718T110000
UID:c8ee01f4f7909e274152eb910c8be3b2@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our fourth Book Club Cohort! Facilitated by Barb D
 os Santos This book club is open to queer and trans participants. Elders a
 nd community members with roots and connections to what is colonially know
 n as Latin America are warmly encouraged to join! Saturdays\, July 18 and 
 25\, August 1 and 8\, 11 am to 1 pm at The 519 [519 Church St.] “Ancestr
 al Future by Ailton Krenak is a book in response to the damage caused by c
 enturies of colonial ravaging and the current ecological\, political and s
 ocial crises\, the leading Indigenous thinker and activist Ailton Krenak w
 arns against the power of corporate capitalism and its destructive impact.
 ” Limited spots\, click on our link in bio. Transit tickets\, snacks\, a
 nd books provided. [Image description\, the cover of Ancestral Future\, an
 d a portrait from Barb dos Santos smiling. In text the details of the prog
 ram] ‍
LOCATION:The 519 Community Centre\, 519 Church Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/latine-book-club
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lesbo Picnic Beach Day for Eastenders
DTSTART:20260718T130000
DTEND:20260718T130000
UID:3f2e520272a31f3728a444192954af9c@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:We are so excited to announce our upcoming Lesbo Picnic Beach 
 Day for all our EastEnders! Whether you&#x27\;re a local or just love a da
 y by the water\, this is the perfect chance to soak up the sun and build c
 ommunity. ☀️ Important Note: This is not a structured event\, so pleas
 e feel free to come and go as you please! Stay for an hour or stay all day
  the choice is yours. We’re also bringing a special guest: a puppy who i
 s learning how to swim! 🐶 If you have a well-behaved pup\, feel free to
  bring them along so they can join the fun. Why you should join: Inclusive
  Space: Bisexuals\, sapphics\, and all queerbies are welcome! Come Solo: D
 on’t have a beach buddy? No problem! I highly encourage you to come alon
 e—most of our attendees do\, and it’s the best way to meet new friends
  and expand your circle. Community Focused: This is all about connecting w
 ith other WLW in the city and enjoying the summer vibes together. The Deta
 ils: 🗓️ Date: July 18th ⏰ Time: 1pm till whenever... 📍 Location:
  Ashbridges Bay 🔗 RSVP: To get exact location closer to the date. Pleas
 e share this post with any queer friends who live in the East End or anyon
 e who has been looking for a community space to connect. Let’s make this
  a day to remember! Follow on instgram for any updates @veryqueertoronto 
 ‍
LOCATION:Beaches Disc Golf at Ashbridges Bay\, 10 Ashbridges Bay Park Rd
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/lesbo-picnic-beach-day-for-eastenders
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
