BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SHANGO W/ Mark Oliver\, Ron Allen\, Kiki LeFreak and Discott
DTSTART:20260725T220000
DTEND:20260725T220000
UID:a0c841549b5312064cdf58a3395838e4@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:SHANGO W/ LOCAL LEGENDS MARK OLIVER\, RON ALLEN\, KIKI LEFREAK
  &amp\; DISCOTT 2 Floors of fun DJs up and downstairs! Shango is Toronto
 ’s favourite underground party for the freaks\, geeks\, queers\, dancers
  and heads! Im very excited to announce a local legend Mr. Mark Oliver! Ba
 ck in 1995 we would see him religiously at Destiny Fridays at Club Generat
 ions on the corner of Isabella and Yonge st. His Dj sets changed my life
 …In the beginning during the summer of 1988\, Mark Oliver inspired by th
 e Second Summer of Love erupting in the UK\, Oliver threw what is widely c
 onsidered Toronto&#x27\;s first ever acid house party — at the Tazmanian
  Ballroom this lit the fuse that would eventually ignite one of the larges
 t rave scenes on the North American continent. In 1991 he was co-running t
 he legendary 23 Hop at 318 Richmond Street West with the Exodus crew. From
  23 Hop he moved to Klub Max on Peter Street — his first foray into a mo
 re mainstream venue. From Klub Max he joined the Exodus crew at the city&#
 x27\;s early warehouse events and outdoor raves\, becoming one of the most
  recognisable names and faces in the growing scene. By 1996 Oliver become 
 the resident DJ at The Guvernment\, one of the most celebrated dance venue
 s in Canadian history. Mark is going to blow our minds with a special Shan
 go curated vinyl set spanning the past present and future! Next up we have
  Ron Allen a local legend for decades\, Toronto’s underground has quietl
 y produced some of the most influential figures in global house and techno
 . Among them stands Ron Allen\, a producer\, DJ\, and label founder whose 
 career traces the evolution of the city’s electronic music scene itself.
  Ron Allen is a Toronto-based\, JUNO-nominated\, music producer\, songwrit
 er\, and DJ. Ron is also the founder of legendary dance music imprint\, St
 robe Records\, an instrumental label in developing the sounds of house mus
 ic and techno in the early 90’s. Co-founding Strobe with Hayden Andre Br
 own\, Ron Allen stands as one of the defining architects of early &#x27\;9
 0s house and techno. A DJ turned producer\, Allen&#x27\;s passion for musi
 c drove him into the studio\, where he crafted tracks that would resonate 
 far beyond the dance floor. Supported by Shango’s founder Kiki LeFreak a
 nd a special vinyl only 4 hour set in the jama by Discott. Thank you every
 one for your continued support and your help in creating a safe and loving
  space for us to be free in! SHANGO is a safe space. PLUR in full effect P
 eace Love Unity and Respect. NO judgement\, homophobia\, racism\, sexual h
 arassment or unwanted touching 10pm to LATE 1.4 hertz &amp\; the jama 961 
 College st ‍
LOCATION:1point4hertz\, 961 College St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/shango-w-mark-oliver-ron-allen-kiki-lefrea
 k-and-discott
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
